	(text "THEORY OF OPERATION  (single channel, Rev D)\nInput: DAC U602 VOUTB (0-2.5 V) -> R401/C403 6.6 us filter -> U402 OPA197 (+16 V / -5 V),\nnon-inverting, gain 1 + R402/R403 = 5.02. DAC 2.390 V = 12.00 V out, 2.500 V = 12.55 V.\nFeedback: AOUT is a sense line tied to V_OUT at the ECU connector, so R414 and the cable\ndrop are inside the loop. If the sense wire opens, R417 closes the loop locally (output ~2 % high).\nStability: C406 47 pF closes a fast local loop round U402; the outer loop through R402 sees\nR414 + cable / ECU capacitance. Phase margin 75 deg at 10 nF, 35 deg at 100 nF.\n\nOUTPUT STAGE\nQ401 BCP56 sources from +16 V through R408 and D401. Q402 BCP53 sinks to -5 V through R410,\nso a pulled-up ECU input is still driven to 0.000 V. R412 keeps ~0.5 mA in Q401 at 0 V and\nR411 carries small signals across the Q401 / Q402 dead band. Headroom: 12 V into 120 R (100 mA)\nwith hFE >= 100 from -40 to 25 C; at 85 C the current limit caps 120 R at about 100 mA.\n\nPROTECTION (hardware only, all continuous)\nSource fold-back (Q405, R408, R415, R416): 52 mA into a short, 90 mA at 6 V, 119 mA at 12 V.\n  Q401 peaks at 0.73 W, so its tab needs the +16 V copper pour.\nSink limit (Q406, R410): ~15 mA. Short to battery up to 32 V: D401 (SS110, 100 V) blocks,\n  Q402 dissipates ~0.5 W.\nD402 SMBJ33A clamps ESD / load dump to ~53 V and negative spikes to -0.7 V.\nFigures: LTspice decks in the sim folder, approximate models, 25 C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 359.41 175.006 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1aa7411a-c892-4e5e-a091-0b5692557980")
	)
	(text "ESD / load dump"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 318.77 218.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "27bc33c2-53ea-4cfb-997d-4ffabffc6518")
	)
	(text "Q406/R410: sink limit ~15 mA (Q402 ~0.5 W with the pin at 32 V, continuous)\nR412 keeps ~0.5 mA through Q401 at 0 V\nR411 carries small signals across the crossover dead band"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
